  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Minimisere. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Minimisere is an original trick-taking card game designed by David Parlett. It is a game of 'controlled winning and losing', where the objective is to win a specific number of tricks (e.g., three or four)â€”or none at allâ€”but avoiding the middle ground and, crucially, avoiding winning everything. It is a tactical game that rewards precise hand evaluation and the ability to 'dump' high cards into other players' tricks.",
    objective: 'Score points by winning exactly 0, 3, or 4 tricks. (Winning 1, 2, or 5 tricks is penalized).',
    gameplay: '1. Must follow suit if possible.\n2. Highest card of led suit wins.\n3. Joker: Can be played on any suit. It wins the trick if led; otherwise, it is neutral (loses).',
